      "other": "I'm thinking that there is utility in maintaining the compiler data (maybe even the AST) semi-persistently.  E.g. if you are loading a library, not having to compile the library code each time will make changing the app's or page's code run faster, no?\n\nAs part of this, we could keep track of what types/files a given file actually uses.  With this, we'd know that \"card\" doesn't depend on anything else, \"deck\" and \"pile\" depend on card, \"solitaire\" depends on them all.  \n\nWhat are the rules for what can modify something else?  E.g. I'd think it is not possible for Solitaire to make changes to card's compile path *without expcliticly saying `a card:...` and extending it.  Is this the case?"
    },
    "q4": {
      "picked": []
    }
  },
  "comments": {
    "q1-A": "Tweaking the auto-generated card in real time is useful for testing/showing off mostly.  You should be able to change the fields, but be told *inline* that the field won't be saved.  Small crossed out floppy icon to the right of the (i) about the field, tip \"You can't save this because it is created automatically.\" etc.\n\n\"All\" edits the type is right, e.g. you should be able to modify the card type by selecting \"All Cards\" and changing the suits.  \n\nSo for \"all cards\", rank should be a type-in field listing the values as pills, same with face, and suit.\nFor derived fields, you'd show the spell to calculate it.\n\nWith the current presentation, you have `clickable when` header over the field, don't repeat `- clickable when ` INSIDE the field.\n\nI'll send more feedback for this in chat where I can past pictures.",
    "q2-A": "Same as above, tooltip would say \"Some can't be changed because they are created automatically.\"  Save the things you can.  (Not sure about this, but let's try it)",
    "q4-A": "The blue \"Card 6 of clubs\" is ALREADY the thing for the card, so we don't need to replicate it.  \"All Cards\" should fit beside."
